# OWNER RULING 2026-08-13: `F` is a BACKING-FIELD convention. It marks a private
# field that backs a property, so the two can share a name (FCount / Count). A
# field on the type's SURFACE backs nothing, and prefixing it would put an
# implementation marker in an API name. So the prefix is required in private and
# strict-private sections only.
#
# This fixture is what makes the replaced heuristic un-reintroducible. The old
# rule asked "is the type T-something?" and honoured that skip only in the
# implicit-first section -- which on a hand-written class exempted
# `Name: TStringList` and `Ready: Boolean` while flagging `Count: Integer`, a
# split with no meaning. Line 5 below (`Tag: Integer`, implicit-first, non-T)
# fired under that rule and must not now.
field-name-prefix 12
field-name-prefix 15
!field-name-prefix 5
!field-name-prefix 7
!field-name-prefix 8
!field-name-prefix 10
!field-name-prefix 13
